tweets.full_text:
Last 5 hrs:

1) My feed was dominated by this X Money / Creator Coin thing. So naturally, an X addict like me, was curious. Everyone was talking about it. So I  replied jokingly to @StarPlatinum_  about it. See below.

2) Then all of a sudden everyone replied to my reply to say go on Pump Fun and take a look now. Ok...

3) To my surprise a coin was created of my handle. Ok silly but fun I guess. I originally posted a screenshot of it at $4k market cap and was like wtf I'm a memecoin now LOL. 

4) Then 1-2 hrs lately it jumped to $1M market cap. Keep in mind I don't have any coins whatsoever and never did. People like @commonsenseplay will continue to say I made $1M off the coin LOL, like what? That's the market cap buddy. Not profit. Fake news. Guy sells $15/sub to tell you to buy $TLT (-25% since his first mention) and $DND.TO (91% since his first mention), rich of him eh?

5) At the same I learned that the creator gets a % of the fees paid directly to their X Money. 

6) I was like cool, donating this to my followers so I don't want to make it seem I'm P&D'ing. How can I if I have no skin in the game. This was just a social experiment. I had no idea it would blow up the way it did. 

7) Buuut I get it, a following like mine with NO history of ever pumping crypto (outside BTC and to some extent ETH) let alone MEME COINS (I've been very vocal against the Trump/Melania coin) can be viewed as not a good look especially to some noobs. For that I am sorry.

8) And with that said I take responsibility and wish I didn't go as far with this as I had with the tweets. Maybe 1-2 tweets to acknowledge it and that is it, but I went overboard with 5-6 tweets. Perhaps the euphoria got to me.

9) And also perhaps my inexperience in this sector (memecoins) got the best of me.

10) Whatever happens to the coin moving forward it's up to the market. The idea behind it sounds intriguing ngl. Something that measures the worth of a social and the value they provide to the free public. But probably if done outside Pump Fun. 

11) That be it.

